 ### [Level-synchronized bisection ray casting](1313-level-synchronized-bisection-ray-casting.md)
-Level-synchronized bisection ray casting is a robust algorithm for rendering the zero-level-set of an implicit function by processing all active rays in lockstep using interval arithmetic to guarantee no surface features are missed. It sets itself apart from its siblings by its specific implementation of level-synchronized processing and Hermite-based root estimation. Choose it when rendering complex implicit scenes requires batched processing and strict feature preservation.
+A robust algorithm that processes all active rays in lockstep using interval arithmetic to guarantee no surface features are missed. It builds on Kalra & Barr by adding level-synchronized processing and Hermite-based root estimation.
 
 ### [Bisection Ray Tracing with Interval Inclusion](1314-bisection-ray-tracing-with-interval-inclusion.md)
-Bisection Ray Tracing with Interval Inclusion is a robust ray-surface intersection algorithm that guarantees finding the nearest intersection of an implicit surface with a ray without missing fine features. It sets itself apart from its siblings by processing rays in batches and using front-to-back pruning to discard intervals behind already found hits. Choose it when occlusion handling and batched interval arithmetic improve performance in multi-surface scenes.
